{"id": "EUVD-2026-86754", "enisaUuid": "ce67fbbc-3f8a-32ac-83bf-4190b9130d6d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/drm_exec: fix up contended obj when num_objects is 0\n\ndrm_exec_prepare_array() silently returns success without calling\ndrm_exec_lock_contended() when num_objects is zero. This breaks the\ninvariant upheld by drm_exec_lock_obj(), where every entry point into\nthe locking sequence must first attempt to lock any previously\ncontended object before proceeding.\n\nDrivers that chain multiple drm_exec_prepare_array() calls per\ndrm_exec_until_all_locked() iteration (e.g. amdgpu's userq signal/wait\nioctls, which prepare separate read and write BO arrays) can pass an\nempty array for one of the two calls. If contention is hit while\npreparing the non-empty array, exec->contended is set and the loop\nretries; on retry, the empty-array call preceding it is a no-op that\nnever clears exec->contended, so drm_exec_retry_on_contention()\nimmediately jumps back to the top of the loop without ever reaching\nthe call that would resolve the contention. This spins forever.\n\nFix it by having drm_exec_prepare_array() call drm_exec_lock_contended()\ndirectly when num_objects is zero, so a pending contended object dont\nloop infinitely.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:22:28", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:10:26", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/506cfed91e50cc8055799480a2fde5a18f63a21c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/831cd124ce99c3e61266bed30519d52f7c26abed", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f3e74866018dab793ebee1fdf0ef34f7271d1f8c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a565022c02f218ec9789c2baf4690792e7a48cbb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/159720704d9d652b64390c11fb971e15b0a78d23"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97900", "GHSA-fx27-pfff-j2g5"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "036238ab-dc03-301f-a5bc-cadcfe2d6e2f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "13929ef9-9fd2-3ad1-a3ac-790e930b5c4c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "15948c46-c8f9-38d6-8398-aa959d37edf2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "09593216bff15866f95c8ad406cb7fdcec1ee40a <a565022c02f218ec9789c2baf4690792e7a48cbb"}, {"id": "5f4d8388-8b25-37da-b1ca-900a0bf5d759", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "09593216bff15866f95c8ad406cb7fdcec1ee40a <506cfed91e50cc8055799480a2fde5a18f63a21c"}, {"id": "61667c3d-0022-309f-93f4-a1307669ef23", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "90ef706b-990e-3bdd-926a-296e5e3cfefc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "97521836-56e6-367e-abd2-2ad10f76a8b8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "09593216bff15866f95c8ad406cb7fdcec1ee40a <159720704d9d652b64390c11fb971e15b0a78d23"}, {"id": "ac137722-b838-3e07-8fb6-171a5781976b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "09593216bff15866f95c8ad406cb7fdcec1ee40a <f3e74866018dab793ebee1fdf0ef34f7271d1f8c"}, {"id": "b4982a92-4cba-3d61-8579-ce8e2def6230", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "bcc517a6-e634-3099-9d1c-544f6d9e5442", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "09593216bff15866f95c8ad406cb7fdcec1ee40a <831cd124ce99c3e61266bed30519d52f7c26abed"}, {"id": "c9fae1ad-3643-3c6c-82c9-fe5539e30ae9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "d1fa1c4a-40f0-33ae-a704-ea7d797bff5d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "27dfe505-a4f4-3f